Yes, but unfortunately, function keys come in two flavors:

Your kind:
  The nice useful kind that you can reprogram to generate any key sequence.

My kind:
  The useless, anal-retentive (but extremely prolific) kind which always
  generates the same sequence of characters, and expects the software to
  understand it's own peculiar nature.

It would be a real nice feature to have.  As far as wasted code, it only needs
to be added to the code for machines which normally have function keys.  And
it can always be a compiler option.

